364: ### Building
365: 
366: This project uses [Chomp](https://chompbuild.com) for building.
367: 
368: With Chomp installed, download the WASI SDK 12.0 from https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/tag/wasi-sdk-12.
369: 
370: - [Linux](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-12/wasi-sdk-12.0-linux.tar.gz)
371: - [Windows (MinGW)](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-12/wasi-sdk-12.0-mingw.tar.gz)
372: - [macOS](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-12/wasi-sdk-12.0-macos.tar.gz)
373: 
374: Locate the WASI-SDK as a sibling folder, or customize the path via the `WASI_PATH` environment variable.
375: 
376: Emscripten emsdk is also assumed to be a sibling folder or via the `EMSDK_PATH` environment variable.
377: 
378: Example setup:
379: 
380: ```
381: git clone https://github.com:guybedford/es-module-lexer
382: git clone https://github.com/emscripten-core/emsdk
383: cd emsdk
384: git checkout 1.40.1-fastcomp
385: ./emsdk install 1.40.1-fastcomp
386: cd ..
387: wget https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk/releases/download/wasi-sdk-12/wasi-sdk-12.0-linux.tar.gz
388: gunzip wasi-sdk-12.0-linux.tar.gz
389: tar -xf wasi-sdk-12.0-linux.tar
390: mv wasi-sdk-12.0-linux.tar wasi-sdk-12.0
391: cargo install chompbuild
392: cd es-module-lexer
393: chomp test
394: ```
395: 
396: For the `asm.js` build, git clone `emsdk` from  is assumed to be a sibling folder as well.
